<Layout title="Privacy on this review website" description="How this LFNYC review site works: no advertising pixels, no analytics cookies, and a contact brief that stays in your browser until you choose to send an email.">
  <div class="shell"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy information · October 9, 2026</p><h1>Clear about<br />your information.</h1><p>This notice describes this LFNYC review website and its contact brief.</p></header><article class="reading"><h2>The contact brief</h2><p>Your entries stay in the current page. The brief does not submit information to a server or save it in browser storage. Preparing a draft creates an email link. Your email provider receives the message only when you choose to send it through your email app.</p><p>Copying the draft puts it on your device’s clipboard. Refreshing or leaving the page may lose what you entered. Do not include passwords, payment details or other sensitive information.</p><h2>Analytics and advertising</h2><p>This site does not load analytics, advertising pixels, tracking cookies or third-party fonts. There is no marketing-consent prompt because there is no marketing tracker to turn on.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>Netlify serves this website. Hosting providers process technical request information, such as an IP address and requested URL, to deliver and protect the service. See <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify’s privacy policy</a> for its practices.</p><h2>Links and messages</h2><p>Links to other websites open services with their own privacy practices. Email, phone and text actions use your chosen communication provider. If you contact Little Fight NYC, the team uses the information you share to respond and discuss the work.</p><h2>Questions about your information</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@littlefightnyc.com">hello@littlefightnyc.com</a> with your question or request. This review site does not create an account, collect payment, or complete a booking.</p></article></div>
</Layout>
